// data.nv - the data of the examples of the package (`examples/`) and of the samples of the specification (`spec/samples/`), compiled into the tests with `embed_str` (a path is read relative to this file):
// the machines of the examples as JSON and as tables, their tests, the registry and the journal of the host "examples" and the registry of the samples. The module is for tests; the program `alula`
// reads the same files from the disk (`alula test examples`). The lists of the files are written by hand (a new file is a new line); a test of `alula.machine_run` fails when a file of the folder is
// missing from its list.
module alula.examples

import alula.machine.{NamedText, Registry, without_journal, load_host}

/// The machines of `examples/` as JSON, by the name of the file (`calc.alula.json`).
export fn machine_files() -> []NamedText => [
    NamedText { name: "actions.alula.json", text: embed_str("../../examples/actions.alula.json") },
